 "notes": [
  "Volumes and capacity are in tonnes; the press release prints lakh tonnes and the statements are in crore, so the constant at the top is 1,00,00,000 rupees in a crore.",
  "The company calls revenue from operations its net sales; cement and its other products (ready-mix concrete, wall putty) are not split, so line 1 is all revenue and line 2 is switched off. The realisation per tonne is revenue over tonnes sold.",
  "The model has no row for exceptional items: the past folds them into other expenses (a cost is added, a gain taken off), so the model's profit before tax is the filing's. FY25's stamp duty on the amalgamation (35.44) is in other expenses.",
  "The filing does not split interest on leases out of finance costs, so all of it is interest on borrowings and the rate on borrowings that comes out is high; interest on leases is left at nil.",
  "Udaipur Cement Works was amalgamated into the company from 1 April 2024 (effective 31 July 2025): the FY25 and H1 FY25 columns are restated, and the share capital rose from 58.85 to 62.09 for the shares issued. Earnings per share as printed is on the weighted shares; the model's is on the shares at each period end.",
  "Freight is a cost of its own (transport, clearing and forwarding), as cement analysts carry it per tonne."
 ],
